(function(){window.PhysicaRankPyqNeet_botany_biodiversityandconservation=[{id:"neet-2026-q091",pn:91,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"Causes of biodiversity loss",q:'"The Evil Quartet" of biodiversity loss includes which of the following?',o:["Over-exploitation; Alien species invasions; Air pollution; Co-extinctions","Habitat loss and fragmentation; over-exploitation; Alien species invasions; Co-extinctions","Habitat loss and fragmentation; Air pollution; Water pollution; Co-extinctions","Over-exploitation; Alien species invasions; Soil pollution; Co-extinctions"],c:1,s:`'The Evil Quartet' is the nickname for the four major causes of biodiversity loss.
They are habitat loss and fragmentation, over-exploitation, alien species invasions and co-extinctions.`},{id:"neet-2026-q095",pn:95,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"Causes of biodiversity loss",q:`Which of the following statements are correct?
A. The Amazon rainforest being cut and cleared for cultivation of soyabeans is an example of habitat loss.
B. Steller's sea cow and passenger pigeon became extinct due to over-exploitation by humans.
C. The Nile perch introduced into Lake Victoria in East Africa helped in population growth of cichlid fish in the lake.
D. Water hyacinth is an invasive species.
E. When a species becomes extinct, the plant and animal species associated with it are not affected.`,o:["B, C and D only","A, B and D only","A, B and E only","C, D and E only"],c:1,s:`The Nile perch introduced into Lake Victoria led to extinction of more than 200 species of cichlid fish, so C is wrong.
When a species becomes extinct, the plant and animal species linked to it in an obligatory way also become extinct, so E is wrong.
Statements A, B and D are correct.`},{id:"neet-2026-q117",pn:117,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"Bioprospecting",q:"Exploring molecular, genetic and species-level diversity for products of economic importance is called",o:["Biomagnification","Biofortification","Bioremediation","Bioprospecting"],c:3,s:"Exploring molecular, genetic and species-level diversity for products of economic importance is called bioprospecting."},{id:"neet-2026-q124",pn:124,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"In situ conservation",q:"Which of the following is an in situ conservation method?",o:["Sacred Groves","Wildlife Safari Parks","Botanical Gardens","Seed Banks"],c:0,s:`In-situ conservation is exemplified by sacred groves.
Wildlife safari parks, botanical gardens and seed banks are examples of ex-situ conservation.
Note: Printed solution text says safari parks, botanical gardens, seed banks are in-situ; this is a slip, they are ex-situ. Printed answer 1 kept.`},{id:"neet-2026-q129",pn:129,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"Mass extinctions",q:"Since the origin and diversification of life on Earth, there have been five episodes of mass extinction of species. How is the sixth extinction, which is in progress, different from the previous episodes?",o:["The current species extinction rates are far lower than those in previous episodes.","The present species extinction rates are 100 to 1000 times faster than in the pre-human times.","The present net species extinction rate is zero.","The current species extinction rate is nearly 10 times faster than previous episodes."],c:1,s:`The current, sixth episode of mass extinction is estimated to be 100 to 1000 times faster than in pre-human times.
Our activities are responsible for these faster rates.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q147",pn:147,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"Species diversity patterns",q:`Arrange the following in descending order of number of species in the Amazonian rain forest.
(a) Plants
(b) Birds
(c) Fishes
(d) Invertebrates
(e) Mammals
Choose the correct answer from the options given below :`,o:["(d) > (a) > (c) > (b) > (e)","(e) > (b) > (a) > (c) > (d)","(b) > (a) > (d) > (c) > (e)","(c) > (b) > (d) > (e) > (a)"],c:0,s:`The Amazonian rain forest has more than 40,000 species of plants.
It has 3,000 species of fishes, 1300 of birds, 427 of mammals and 378 of reptiles.
It has more than 1,25,000 invertebrates.
So the decreasing order is (d) > (a) > (c) > (b) > (e).`},{id:"neet-2025-q099",pn:99,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"Ex-situ conservation",q:"Which one of the following is an example of ex-situ conservation?",o:["National Park","Wildlife Sanctuary","Zoos and botanical gardens","Protected areas"],c:2,s:`Zoological parks (zoos), botanical gardens and wildlife safari parks are examples of ex-situ conservation.
Sacred groves, biosphere reserves, national parks and wildlife sanctuaries are examples of in-situ conservation.`},{id:"neet-2025-q164",pn:164,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"Conservation terms",q:`Match List I with List II:
List I \u2014 List II
A. The Evil Quartet \u2014 I. Cryopreservation
B. Ex situ conservation \u2014 II. Alien species invasion
C. Lantana camara \u2014 III. Causes of biodiversity losses
D. Dodo \u2014 IV. Extinction
Choose the option with all correct matches.`,o:["A-III, B-II, C-I, D-IV","A-III, B-I, C-II, D-IV","A-III, B-IV, C-II, D-I","A-III, B-II, C-IV, D-I"],c:1,s:`The Evil Quartet - causes of biodiversity losses.
Ex situ conservation - cryopreservation.
Lantana camara - alien species invasion.
Dodo - extinction.`},{id:"neet-2024-q102",pn:102,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"Ex-situ conservation",q:"The type of conservation in which the treatened species are taken out from their naturaly habitat and placed in special setting where they can be protected and given special care is called",o:["Semi-conservative method","Sustainable development","in-situ conservation","Biodiversity conservation"],c:3,s:`Taking threatened species out of their natural habitat and placing them in special settings for protection and care is ex-situ conservation.
Ex-situ conservation is a type of biodiversity conservation.
So the printed answer is option (4).`},{id:"neet-2024-q109",pn:109,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"Species richness in tropics",q:`Tropical regions show greatest level of species richness because
(A) Tropical latitudes have remained relatively undisturbed for milions of years, hence more time was available for species diversification.
(B) Tropical environments are more seasonal
(C) More solar energy is available in tropics
(D) Constant environments promote niche specialization.
(E) Tropical environments are constant and predictable.
Choose the correct answer form the options given below :`,o:["A, B and E only","A, B and D only","A, C, D and E only","A and B only"],c:2,s:`Only statement B is wrong.
Unlike temperate regions, tropical environments are less seasonal, fairly constant and predictable.
So A, C, D and E are correct.`},{id:"neet-2024-q112",pn:112,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"Causes of biodiversity loss",q:`These are regarded as major causes of biodiversity loss :
(A) Over exploitation  (B) Co-extinction  (C) Mutation
(D) Habitat loss and fragmentation  (E) Migration
Choose the correct option :`,o:["A, B and E only","A, B and D only","A, C and D only","A, B, C and D only"],c:1,s:`The major causes of biodiversity loss are:
(1) alien species invasions
(2) co-extinctions
(3) habitat loss and fragmentation
(4) over-exploitation.
Mutation and migration are not on this list.
So the correct option is A, B and D only.`},{id:"neet-2024-q135",pn:135,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"Conservation organisations",q:"List of endangered species was released by-:",o:["Foam","IUCN","GEAC","WWF"],c:1,s:"The list of endangered species is released by IUCN."},{id:"neet-2024-q148",pn:148,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"Biodiversity scientists",q:`Match List-I with List-II.
A. Robert May \u2014 I. Species area relationship
B. Alexander von Humboldt \u2014 II. Long term ecosystem experiment using out door plots
C. Paul Ehrlich \u2014 III. Global species diversity at about 7 million
D. David Tilman \u2014 IV. Rivet popper hypothesis
Choose the correct answer from the options given below`,o:["A-I, B-III, C-II, D-IV","A-III, B-IV, C-II, D-I","A-II, B-III, C-I, D-IV","A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II"],c:3,s:`Robert May put global species diversity at about 7 million.
Alexander von Humboldt described the species-area relationship.
Paul Ehrlich used the rivet popper analogy to show the role of species in an ecosystem.
David Tilman did long term ecosystem experiments using outdoor plots.
So A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II.`},{id:"neet-2023-q116",pn:116,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"Earth Summit and conservation",q:`The historic Convention on Biological Diversity. "The Earth Summit' was held in Rio de Janeiro in the year :`,o:["2002","1985","1992","1986"],c:2,s:`The Convention on Biological Diversity, the Earth Summit, was held in Rio de Janeiro in 1992.
It asked all nations to take steps to conserve biodiversity and use its benefits sustainably.`},{id:"neet-2023-q129",pn:129,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"The Evil Quartet",q:"Among \u2018The Evil Quartet\u2019, which one is considered the most important cause driving extinction of species?",o:["Co-extinctions","Habitat loss and fragmentation","Over exploitation for economic gain","Alien species invasions"],c:1,s:"Habitat loss and fragmentation is the most important cause driving plants and animals to extinction."},{id:"neet-2022-q101",pn:101,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"Ex situ conservation",q:"Which of the following is not a method of ex situ conservation?",o:["National Parks","Micropropagation","Cryopreservation","In vitro fertilization"],c:0,s:`In-situ conservation protects the whole ecosystem on site.
National parks are in-situ conservation.
Micropropagation, cryopreservation and in-vitro fertilisation are ex-situ methods.`},{id:"neet-2022-q119",pn:119,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"Causes of biodiversity loss",q:"Habitat loss and fragmentation, over exploitation, alien species invasion and co-extinction are causes for:",o:["Competition","Biodiversity loss","Natality","Population explosion"],c:1,s:"These four are the main causes of biodiversity loss."},{id:"neet-2022-q139",pn:139,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"CNG and air pollution",q:"The entire fleet of buses in Delhi were converted to CNG from diesel. In reference to this, which one of the following statements is false?",o:["The same diesel engine is used in CNG buses making the cost of conversion low","It is cheaper than diesel","It cannot be adulterated like diesel","CNG burns more efficiently than diesel"],c:0,s:`CNG is cheaper than diesel and petrol.
It burns more efficiently.
It cannot be adulterated like diesel or petrol.
The same diesel engine cannot be used for CNG buses, so statement (1) is false.`},{id:"neet-2022-q156",pn:156,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"In-situ conservation",q:"In-situ conservation refers to:",o:["Conserve only high-risk species","Conserve only endangered species","Conserve only extinct species","Protect and conserve the whole ecosystem"],c:3,s:`In-situ (on-site) conservation protects the whole ecosystem.
This protects biodiversity at all levels.`},{id:"neet-2022-q186",pn:186,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Biodiversity and Conservation",st:"Air pollution control",q:"Given below are two statements: Statements I: In a scrubber the exhaust from the thermal plant is passed through the electric wires to charge the dust particles. Statement II: Particulate matter (PM 2.5) cannot be removed by scrubber but can be removed by an electrostatic precipitator. In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the option given below:",o:["Both Statement I and Statement II are in correct","Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect","Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct","Both Statement I and Statement II are correct"],c:2,s:`A scrubber removes gases like SO2 by passing exhaust through a limestone slurry. It does not use electric wires, so Statement I is wrong.
The electrostatic precipitator charges dust particles with electric wires and removes about 99% of particulate matter, even PM 2.5.
So Statement II is correct.`}]})();
